; The ONE variable: `layout_direction = 3` (RTL) on a RichTextLabel.
; `_draw_line`'s own alignment switch (rich_text_label.cpp:987-1014) branches on
; the PARAGRAPH direction — `l.text_buf->get_direction()`, set from
; `_find_direction` (:599,3507-3525), which returns is_layout_rtl() only while
; `text_direction` is INHERITED. Its default is TEXT_DIRECTION_AUTO
; (rich_text_label.h:615), so `layout_direction` alone reaches none of those
; arms and each RTL row must land exactly where its LTR twin does. Every label
; spans the full viewport width so its OWN rect mirror (control.cpp:1785) is
; the identity. No other fixture pairs a RichTextLabel with a direction, so a
; swap wired to the layout direction instead is invisible everywhere else.
